{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1534762-fan-content-taimen-of-the-rivers","id":1534762,"title":"Fan Content: Taimen of the Rivers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-04-26T09:05:59-07:00","id":1534762,"title":"Fan Content: Taimen of the Rivers","content":"Here is a first attempt at creating something for Exalted 3e. Inspired by the animals found in Many Faces Strangers, I thought I'd try my hand at creating an animal. I plan on using this in one of my upcoming Lunar games. The animal itself is based on the Siberian taimen (Hucho <i>taimen</i>) and the prehistoric spike toothed salmon (<i>Oncorhynchus rastrosus</i>). Along with a bit at the end on making the more common salmonids (subfamily Salmoninae).<br /> <br /> Obviously comments for improvement are much appreciated.<br /> <br /> <b>Taimen</b><br /> Swimming up the rivers all across the northern reaches of Creation large salmon inhabit the cold rivers and oceans providing a bounteous resource for local populations at specific times of the year. These fish grow to enormous size in the northern oceans, reaching eight feet long and over 200 pounds.<br /> <br /> In the ocean, these fish have gleaming silver scales with some having a black back or speckled sides. When swimming upriver to spawn they undergo dramatic physical changes. The silver turns bright red, or brown with bright spots and other accents. Males grow a vicious hooked skype to fight rivals and guard redds. After spawning, taimen in the North and Northwest return to the ocean, losing their breeding colors until the next year; in the Northeast most of the breeding adults die and their bodies amplify the fertility of the region.<br /> <br /> All across the North, these fish and their smaller cousins form a key piece of peoples foodways. The annual fish runs occur during the season of Wood, peaking in Resplendent Wood. Many groups have rites and ceremonies around the annual return of these fish with the fishing season taking on a festival air. A wide array of techniques are used to hunt these fish from spears (gigging), to fixed and floating nets to semi-permanent structures in the rivers.<br /> <br /> Once caught the fish are either eaten fresh or prepared for storage. Smoking and salting are the most popular ways to preserve them and make for valuable exports for the more refined preparations.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Essence: 1; Willpower: 1; Join Battle: 3 dice</b><br /> <b>Health Levels: -1/-2/-4/Incap. </b>Taimen will fight until they take three health levels of damage<br /> <b>Actions: </b>Senses: 6 dice (see Aquatic Vision, Keen Nose); Swimming: 10 dice, Tracking: 7 dice (homing instinct)<br /> Resolve 1, Guile 1<br /> <br /> <b>Combat</b><br /> <b>Attack (Bite): 4 dice (Damage 1L; 6L against enemies the taimen\u2019s size or smaller)</b><br /> <b>Combat Movement: 10 dice</b><br /> Evasion 5, Parry 1<br /> <b>Soak/Hardness: 3/0</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Special Abilities</b><br /> <b>Ambush Hunter: </b>Add three dice on unexpected attack rolls.<br /> <br /> <b>Merits</b><br /> <b>Aquatic Grace: </b>While underwater, double 9\u2019s on movement actions and gain +2 Evasion.<br /> <b>Aquatic Vision: T</b>he eyes of the taimen are well suited to perceiving threats both below and above the waves. The salmon gains three dice to notice movement in either environment. They use this to both hunt prey and avoid being prey themselves.<br /> <b>Keen Nose: </b>Double 9s on scent-based Sense rolls underwater.<br /> <br /> <b>Salmon/Trout/Char</b><br /> Smaller cousins of the human sized Taimen. Salmon are even more prolific in Northern waters. They come in a dazzling array of markings that are very localized and highly sought after by anglers of leisure. Some local economies make fairly comfortable livings escorting fishermen on long treks into the wilderness to find elusive breeds. Noteworthy breeds include the Bloodgill, of the Skullstone Archipelago to the bright yellow Flaxen Trout in the Northeast.<br /> <br /> <br /> These fish use the same traits as the taimen but apply the Tiny Creature Merit.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Lead Writer for the Savage Age of Werewolf: the Apocalypse: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/428750/Ghost-Lineages-The-Advanced-Players-Guide-to-the-Savage-Age\" target=\"_blank\">Ghost Lineages</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/312700/The-Rise-of-the-Garou-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Two\" target=\"_blank\">Rise of the Garou</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/331302/Tools-of-Extinction-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Three\" target=\"_blank\">Tools of Extinction</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/352717/Tribebook-Wlewa\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook: Wlewa</a>.<br /> <br /> Want RPGs in libraries? Check out my book, <a href=\"http://www.abc-clio.com/ABC-CLIOCorporate/product.aspx?pc=A3951P\" target=\"_blank\">Dragons in the Stacks</a>. Now with <a href=\"http://www.ennie-awards.com/blog/2015-ennie-award-nominees-and-spotlight-winners/\" target=\"_blank\">awards</a>!<br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":1813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","user":"grimjaws","date":". 04-26-2024, 12:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","name":"grimjaws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1813_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-28T13:33:50-07:00","id":1534858,"title":"","content":"So they're like salmon sized piranhas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-